   "t": 1319,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/pp2pppp/2Np1n2/8/4P3/3B4/PPP2PPP/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 0 6",
   "line": [
    "Nxc6"
   ],
   "spoken": "Provoke the trade on c6 by developing the knight there. In the Sicilian, trading off the d4-knight is almost always good for Black — it hands over the centre and opens lines.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": "In the Sicilian, exchanging White's d4-knight favours Black nearly every time.",
   "plans": "Recapture toward the centre and open the b-file."
  },
  {
   "ply": 12,
   "t": 1320,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/p3pppp/2pp1n2/8/4P3/3B4/PPP2PPP/RNBQK2R w KQkq - 0 7",
   "line": [
    "bxc6"
   ],
   "spoken": "Recapture with the b-pawn: Black gets a mobile central pawn mass and a semi-open b-file. Not decisive on their own, but a pleasant, flexible position with clear plans.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": "Recapturing toward the centre trades structure for mobility and an open file.",
   "plans": "Fianchetto, castle, and roll the centre."
  },
  {
   "ply": 13,
   "t": 1330,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/p3pppp/2pp1n2/8/2P1P3/3B4/PP3PPP/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 0 7",
   "line": [
    "c4"
